-- title:
--   Left exactness of Jacobi–Zariski for Koszul-acyclic presentations
-- statement:
--   Let $R$, $S$, $T$ be commutative rings with $S$ an $R$-algebra and $T$ both an $R$-algebra and an $S$-algebra, the two structures being compatible via the scalar tower $R \to S \to T$, and assume $T$ is flat as an $S$-module. Let $\iota$ be an index type and $x : \iota \to T$ a family of elements such that the $S$-algebra homomorphism $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}\ \iota\ S \to T$ evaluating the variables at $x$ is surjective. Let $n \in \mathbb{N}$ and $f : \mathrm{Fin}\ n \to \mathrm{MvPolynomial}\ \iota\ S$ be such that the kernel of this evaluation homomorphism is the ideal generated by the range of $f$, so that $T \cong S[X_i ; i \in \iota]/(f_1,\dots,f_n)$. Assume further that all syzygies among the $f_j$ are Koszul: for every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\ n \to \mathrm{MvPolynomial}\ \iota\ S$ with $\sum_j c_j f_j = 0$ there exists a family $d_{jl}$ of polynomials with $d_{jj} = 0$ and $d_{jl} = -d_{lj}$ for all $j, l$, satisfying $c_j = \sum_l f_l\, d_{jl}$ for all $j$. Then the $T$-linear map $T \otimes_S H_1(L_{S/R}) \to H_1(L_{T/R})$ obtained from `Algebra.H1Cotangent.map R R S T` by base change along $S \to T$ is injective, where $H_1(L_{-/-})$ denotes the first homology of the naive cotangent complex.
--
--   This is the left-exactness end of the Jacobi–Zariski sequence for $R \to S \to T$ when $T$ is a flat $S$-algebra presented by polynomials whose first Koszul homology vanishes; the hypothesis on syzygies is precisely what the argument consumes, and is weaker than requiring $f_1,\dots,f_n$ to be a regular sequence. It is used to derive the corresponding statement under a Zariski-local weak regularity hypothesis, [`Algebra.injective_liftBaseChange_h1CotangentMap_of_span_eq_top_of_forall_exists_isWeaklyRegular`](thm.html#Algebra.injective_liftBaseChange_h1CotangentMap_of_span_eq_top_of_forall_exists_isWeaklyRegular).
